  - [1mAdd a bundler[0m — rejected; this repo has zero dependencies and no build step, and nothing here needs one.

  I lean toward the plain script and a global. Normally I'd argue for real modules, but the deciding factor is that this
  page has exactly one consumer today and the module switch buys enforcement at the cost of breaking the simplest way
  to run the app. The global is also not a dead end: moving one file from a global to an [38;5;153mexport[39m later is mechanical, and
  the future forms you mentioned are the natural moment to pay for it.

[38;5;246m⏺ [39mUser answered Claude's questions:
[38;5;246m  ⎿  · How should the store be wired into the page? → Plain script + global (Recommended)[39m

[38;5;231m⏺[39m Last question before I present the design. This repo has no configured tooling at all — no linter, no formatter, no
  test runner, zero dependencies. Setting that up is cheapest now, before the subsystem exists, and whatever you pick
  lands in the spec's Global Constraints so every later task inherits it.

  One design consequence worth knowing while you choose: [38;5;153msessionStorage[39m doesn't exist in Node, so for the store to be
  unit-testable at all, it has to take its storage backend as an injectable that defaults to [38;5;153msessionStorage[39m. That's a
  small, worthwhile shape change I'd fold into the design if you want unit tests — and it's also just better isolation.
  If you skip tests, I'd keep the injectable anyway but nothing would exercise it.

